      <Desc>In the San Diego Master Chorales 64th season, over 13,000 audience members were served through four self-produced concerts and seven performances with artistic partners (San Diego Symphony, Salvation Army) and thousands more were reached through radio and television broadcasts of performances on KPBS 89.5 FM and a Holiday Special on KPBS. The Chorale partnered with the Choral Consortium of San Diego and Beer Choir San Diego to present a community sing with over 150 community members who joined together in song. The Chorale appeared on the first concert in the new Jacobs Music Center after a large-scale renovation. The season set a new attendance record for the season, a new all-time sales record, and saw a 40% increase in overall attendance over the previous season.</Desc>
